My current simple workaround is to catch `-h` before cobra takes over:

```go
[..]
        rootCmd.SetUsageTemplate(strings.TrimSpace(usage) + "\n")

        if slices.Contains(os.Args, "-h") {
                fmt.Println(shortusage)
                os.Exit(0)
        }

        err := rootCmd.Execute()
        if err != nil {
                os.Exit(1)
        }
```
